{
  "configuration_id": "config_039",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_038 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, concat) is our best result at 0.721 acc, a ~7-point jump over the best RNA-only (config_006, 0.653). Image-only models are very weak (0.21–0.23), so the multimodal gain likely comes from complementary rather than independently predictive image features. Uncertainty: we do not yet know whether the concat fusion in config_038 is optimal or whether a weighted fusion would better balance the strong RNA signal against the weak image signal. Question: config_039 is identical to config_038 except fusion=weighted vs concat, isolating the fusion strategy as the single variable. Why best next experiment: it is a clean one-parameter A/B against our current best, directly testing whether the fusion mechanism is a critical design lever. If weighted substantially outperforms concat, it tells us the weaker image modality should be down-weighted and reshapes all future multimodal choices; if the two are comparable, it tells us fusion method is not a key factor and we should pivot to testing image encoder or aggregation. This is the highest-information-per-experiment choice under the limited budget."
}

